## Web code style

Architecture judgment lives in the root [principles](../../../../.cursor/rules/principles.mdc) rule. This file is web implementation style only.

- Write concise, technical TypeScript with accurate examples.
- Prefer functional and declarative patterns; avoid classes.
- Prefer iteration and modularization over duplication.
- Use descriptive names with auxiliary verbs (e.g. `isLoading`, `hasError`).
- Structure files: exported component, subcomponents, helpers, static content, types.
- Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/) for commits and pull request titles.
